 {
  "tag": "travel",
  "hub": {
   "hub_name": "travel",
   "tag_id": "travel",
   "background_color": "#438017",
   "header_image": "/static/images/tag_headers/travel.jpg",
   "header_link": "",
   "post_id": "828522450437406720",
   "blog_name": "",
   "blog_avatar": "",
   "followers_count": "26M",
   "followers_count_int": 25631208,
   "new_posts_count": "402",
   "new_posts_count_int": 402,
   "post_count_int": 0,
   "editorial_description": "<p><em>Frank Sinatra sang</em> “Let’s take a boat to <a href=\"http://marmastewbeck.wordpress.com/2010/09/30/and-a-bit-more/\" target=\"_blank\">Bermuda</a>/let’s take a plane to <a href=\"http://lindastaatsphoto.wordpress.com/2010/08/22/the-fog-comes/\" target=\"_blank\">St. Paul</a>/let’s get away from it all! ” To travel is to give into wanderlust — regardless of how you define it. You may crave a <a href=\"http://domestiphobia.net/2010/10/26/chasin-waterfalls/\" target=\"_blank\">wild adventure</a> or simply want to admire <a href=\"http://beingmark.com/2010/10/08/a-little-blue/\" target=\"_blank\">mother nature </a>from the serenity of a hammock. You may love the thrill of jumping on the <a href=\"http://obblogato.wordpress.com/2010/10/28/pollution-free/\" target=\"_blank\">subway</a> in a gigantic city or instead dream of <a href=\"http://thosecrazycanfields.com/2010/10/28/sailing-in-paradise/\" target=\"_blank\">kayaking</a> down a solitary <a href=\"http://hollyyurchisonphotography.wordpress.com/2010/10/30/ohio-river-at-ripley-and-augusta-ky-ferry/\" target=\"_blank\">river</a>. In other words, “Let’s leave our hut, dear/Get out of our rut, dear/Let’s get away from it all.”</p>",
   "editorial_description_text": "Frank Sinatra sang “Let’s take a boat to Bermuda/let’s take a plane to St. Paul/let’s get away from it all! ” To travel is to give into wanderlust — regardless of how you define it. You may crave a wild adventure or simply want to admire mother nature from the serenity of a hammock. You may love the thrill of jumping on the subway in a gigantic city or instead dream of kayaking down a solitary river. In other words, “Let’s leave our hut, dear/Get out of our rut, dear/Let’s get away from it all.”"
  },
